          <p class="sub reveal d2">
            Every other path asks your users to adapt to a new SDK. Ferrule is the only one that treats your existing
            SDK as the specification.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="cmp reveal">
          <div class="cmp-scroll">
            <table>
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th></th>
                  <th class="us"><b>Ferrule</b>open toolkit on Forge</th>
                  <th><b>Open-core generator</b>free tier</th>
                  <th><b>Hosted platform</b>closed, subscription</th>
                  <th><b>Freeze &amp; hand-maintain</b>do nothing</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody>
                <tr>
                  <th>Reads your stainless.yml as-is</th><td class="us y">Validated against the public schema</td><td
                    class="n">No</td
                  ><td class="m">Partly</td><td>n/a</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th>Same Python your users import</th><td class="us y">Identical, by design</td><td class="n"
                    >Its own style</td
                  ><td class="m">Close</td><td class="y">Until the spec changes</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th>Proof nothing broke</th><td class="us y"><code>ferrule verify</code></td><td class="n">No</td><td
                    class="n">No</td
                  ><td class="n">No</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th>Licence of generated code</th><td class="us y">Yours, no obligations</td><td class="n"
                    >Copyleft on free path</td
                  ><td class="m">Vendor terms</td><td class="y">Yours</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th>Account, token or login</th><td class="us y">None</td><td class="n">Required</td><td class="n"
                    >Required</td
                  ><td class="y">None</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th>Runs offline, in your CI</th><td class="us y">Laptop, CI, air-gapped</td><td class="m"
                    >With a key</td
                  ><td class="n">Hosted</td><td class="y">Yes</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th>Keeps your hand edits</th><td class="us y">Patches, re-applied three-way</td><td class="m"
                    >Partly</td
                  ><td class="m">Partly</td><td class="y">Manually</td>
                </tr>
                <tr>
                  <th>Keeps up with the spec</th><td class="us y">PR with a semver label</td><td class="y">Yes</td><td
