          <h2 class="h2 reveal d1">We publish the scoreboard. <em>Even the red.</em></h2>
          <p class="sub reveal d2">
            {board.length} real Stainless Python SDKs, pinned at their last Stainless commit and regenerated by Ferrule.
            Ferrule is pre-alpha: this board is how you'll know when yours is ready.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="board reveal">
          <div class="board-head">
            <span>SDK</span><span>Repository</span><span>Breaking</span><span>Text closeness</span><span>Own tests</span>
          </div>
          <div id="boardRows">
            {
              board.map((r) => (
                <div class:list={['brow', { 'hero-row': r.breaking === 0 && r.tests_status === 'passed' }]}>
                  <span class="nm">{r.name}</span>
                  <span class="rp">{r.repo ?? '—'}</span>
                  <span class:list={['br', r.breaking === 0 ? 'zero' : 'non']}>
                    {r.breaking}
                    {r.additive > 0 && <span class="add"> · +{r.additive}</span>}
                  </span>
                  <span class="bar-wrap">
                    <span class="bar">
                      <i data-w={r.closeness ?? 0} />
                    </span>
                    <span>{r.closeness ? `${r.closeness.toFixed(1)}%` : 'n/a'}</span>
                  </span>
                  <span class:list={['ts', { p: r.tests_status === 'passed' }]}>{testsLabel(r)}</span>
                </div>
              ))
            }
          </div>
          <div class="board-foot">
            <span>{boardDate ? `Generated ${boardDate}` : 'Regenerated nightly'} · target for every row: 0 breaking</span>
            <a href={`${docs}fidelity/`}>Full board and methodology →</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="sec faq flush" id="faq">
      <div class="wrap faq-grid">
        <div>
          <div class="kicker reveal">Questions</div>
          <h2 class="h2 reveal d1">The fine print, <em>in plain words.</em></h2>
        </div>
        <div class="reveal d1">
          <details open>
            <summary>Will my users have to change any code?<span class="pm"></span></summary>
            <div class="ans">
              No, and Ferrule checks that for you. <code>ferrule verify</code> diffs the public API of the new output
              against your last Stainless release, and adoption runs it before anything is committed. The GitHub Action
              fails if a breaking change arrives without a label.
            </div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What happens to the code we wrote by hand?<span class="pm"></span></summary>
            <div class="ans">
              Adoption records every hand edit to a generated file as a patch under <code>.ferrule/patches/</code> and
              re-applies it three-way on each regeneration. Your <code>lib/</code> folder and <code>keep_files</code> are
              never touched. If a patch no longer applies, the run stops with <code>FER4102</code> and names the file.
            </div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is the generated SDK really ours?<span class="pm"></span></summary>
            <div class="ans">
              Yes. In adopt mode the runtime is copied from your own repository, so it stays under the licence you
              already ship. The SDK has no dependency on Ferrule or Forge, and the generated code carries no
              obligations.
            </div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Is Ferrule affiliated with Stainless or Cloudflare?<span class="pm"></span></summary>
            <div class="ans">
              No. Ferrule is an independent Apache-2.0 project. It uses Cloudflare's open-source Forge engine as a
              pinned dependency, and treats public Stainless-generated SDKs (which are Apache-2.0) as the reference
              output.
            </div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>How ready is it?<span class="pm"></span></summary>
            <div class="ans">
              Pre-alpha. The converter, plugin and runtime are done, and the OneBusAway SDK regenerates with zero
              breaking changes and all 1,110 of its own tests passing. It isn't on PyPI yet: the
              <a href={`${docs}quickstart/`}>quickstart</a> shows how to run it from source. Watch the fidelity board
              for your kind of SDK.
            </div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>Only Python?<span class="pm"></span></summary>
            <div class="ans">
              For now, on purpose. One language done perfectly beats four done approximately. TypeScript comes after
              Python is proven, and only if teams ask for it.
            </div>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary>What does it cost?<span class="pm"></span></summary>
            <div class="ans">
              Nothing. Everything that runs on your machine is open source. If there is ever a paid offering, it will be
              optional services like fixed-fee migrations with a signed fidelity report, never a token you need to
              generate code.
            </div>
          </details>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

